d, intensity, conditions, result and limitations. Deduct material exactly once; record consumed or altered sample as spent material/residue rather than returning it as pristine edible stock. Reusable tools remain real tools and are not duplicated. On cancellation, interruption or actor death, stop the action, preserve only completed observations, charge only actually incurred costs and leave surviving unconsumed material subject to normal inventory rules; do not refund spent energy or consumed material. Any reservation must be released once, without creating stock. No autonomous ongoing investigation, maintenance obligation or continuing benefit is created. Actual heating or other independently existing processes retain their own rules. Development/review waiting advances no world time. Execute these constraints in code rather than by repeated model approval; record reuse of the referenced handlers, not reinvention. Public availability does not grant Kai mastery, resources or permission.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":0,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Functional findings and experience are separate. This review, the request, reading a contract, registration and learning yield no experience benefit. A completed, personally applicable observation may qualify only if it verifiably adds information, including a genuinely informative failure; repeating an unchanged query or unsupported conclusion does not. Familiar legitimate hands-on practice may sustain modest benefit only through actual participation, not merely invocation. Use only an already implemented bounded experience rule with functional deduplication, an explicit cap, decay and cooldown; if none applies, grant no new pleasure or satisfaction effect in this reuse decision. No food nutrition, health gain or comfort increase is supplied by probing. Physical comfort remains capped at 10, nutrition is not reduced by mood, and protected reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions are unchanged.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Use observable execution events and reusable metadata identifying operation, actual target, mode, intensity, progress/status and recorded outcome. Show inspection or a physical manipulation only when it actually occurs; show wetting or heating only when its physical prerequisites are present and used. Retain sample identity, method and uncertainty with any displayed finding. An interrupted, blocked, failed or inconclusive action must be displayed as such, never with a success indicator or a safe-to-eat badge. Display no toxin, nutrition or preparation annotation unless a supporting measurement actually established it. Presentation alone supplies neither a functional effect nor experience credit.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

